==
== <Recipe> attributes:
==   Enabled            1 = active, 0 = skip this recipe entirely.
==   Type               Native handler ID (fixed per built-in mix - do not
==                       change on an existing recipe).
==   RecipeID           Unique ID within this Type's handler. Falls back to
==                       MixID if omitted.
==   ClientSync         1 = client shows this recipe in the Chaos Machine UI
==                       and its Requirements/Rates/Result below are enforced
==                       server-side too. 0 = display-only; the native
==                       hardcoded handler's own check still runs (Money and
==                       Rates below are then informational only).
==   Name               Recipe name shown to the player.
==   PriceType          0 Zen, 1 WCoinC, 2 WCoinP, 3 GoblinPoint,
==                       4 GensContribution.
==   Money              Zen/coin cost. -1 keeps the native handler's own
==                       dynamic price formula (only valid when Type>=0).
==   DailyLimit         Max uses per account per day. 0 = unlimited.
==   RequireCastleOwner 1 = only the current Castle Siege owning guild's
==                       members can use this recipe.
==   RequireGuildMaster 1 = only a guild master can use this recipe.
==   ResultBag          Optional EventItemBagManager.xml Bag Index to roll
==                       the result from instead of a fixed Result. -1 = none.
==   Mode               "Fixed" (default) or "Evolution".
==
== <Rates AL0-3=".."/> success rate percent per Ancient Level (0-3) of the
==   crafted item, read by the native handler for its own formula.
==
== <Result Section="" Index="" Level="" /> the crafted item (Mode="Fixed").
==
== <Requirements><Item .../></Requirements> - materials consumed:
==   Section/Index      Item (matches Item.xml).
==   MinLevel/MaxLevel  Required item level range. -1 = any.
==   Count              How many are required.
==   CountMode          0 = that many item slots, 1 = Level+1 stacks
==                       (jewels), 2 = raw Durability units (potions/etc).
==   MinDurability/MaxDurability  -1 = any.
==   Role="EvolutionItem"  Marks which requirement is the base item being
==                       evolved (Mode="Evolution" only).
==
== Mode="Evolution" only:
==   <EvolutionMap><Item FromSection="" FromIndex="" ToSection="" ToIndex=""
==     ResultLevel="" /></EvolutionMap>  what the EvolutionItem turns into.
==   <InheritOptions Level="" Durability="" Skill="" Luck=""
==     AdditionalOption="" ExcellentOptions="" AncientOptions=""
==     HarmonyOptions="" Option380="" SocketOptions="" />  1 = carry that
==     property over from the base item to the result.
==   <Failure DestroyEvolutionItem="" DestroyMaterials="" ReduceLevel="" />
==     what happens on the small failure chance implied by Rates.
== Modify only if you know what you're doing!
============================================================
-->
